Subject: Cantor Seeded Compiler Slice 8 Lifecycle Validation MCP Justification

@ [justification_uuid] 6f196fce-dba4-423b-9f9c-2cbbea2db737
@ [source_uuid] 526cea59-fda0-47ff-9dac-12ccc7c59d39
@ [canonical_uuid] 90a93873-f7da-4d6f-ad48-563a138734a7

& [Problem]
  + Slice7 is callable from a local process but not yet discoverable as an inference tool

& [Selection]
  + a separate stateless stdio MCP server gives Codex llama.cpp-compatible hosts and other agents one standard tool seam while reusing exact core semantics

& [Isolation]
  + a new crate avoids changing the existing signed-corpus query server and its mode-dependent published tool list

& [Safety]
  + typed bounded arguments direct delegation caller-owned state structured response and no ambient providers preserve Slice7 authority

& [Deferred]
  + host installation content-addressed request compression runtime state and production effects require separate specifications
